# R2 on the GPU window (W4-WIN-CLOSE C2): the view and the surface. A change committed while the view
# is elsewhere is Offscreen and is never waited for; a change that was in view and is left behind is
# OutOfView and is not satisfied by frames that do not draw it; a new surface epoch (a resize) does
# not let an earlier frame count. Run with --gpu. Every `expect` fails the session if not met.
look 1052 444
key b
select 1307
rotate 0
wait frames 90

# ---- committed while the view is elsewhere: Offscreen (the publication is held until it moved) -
hold publication
click 1052 444
wait held
look 1160 520
wait frames 20
release publication
wait outcome
wait drawn
expect visibility Offscreen
look 1052 444
wait frames 40
expect visibility Offscreen
checkpoint offscreen_settled

# ---- in view, then left behind: OutOfView, and back in view waits for the chunks again ---------
hold chunks
click 1068 444
wait outcome
wait blocked
wait frames 20
expect visibility ChunksStale
look 1160 520
wait frames 30
expect visibility OutOfView
checkpoint out_of_view
look 1052 444
wait frames 30
expect visibility ChunksStale
checkpoint back_in_view_stale
release chunks
wait drawn
expect visibility Visible
checkpoint view_visible

# ---- a new surface epoch while the change waits: frames of the old epoch do not count -----------
hold chunks
click 1076 444
wait outcome
wait blocked
wait frames 20
expect visibility ChunksStale
checkpoint before_resize
resize 1100 640
wait frames 40
expect visibility ChunksStale
checkpoint after_resize
release chunks
wait drawn
expect visibility Visible
checkpoint resized_visible

# ---- no visual change: a refused command and a demolish of an empty tile ----------------------
click 1076 444
wait outcome
expect outcome Refused Occupied
wait drawn
expect visibility NoVisualChange
key x
click 1100 444
wait outcome
expect outcome Applied
wait drawn
expect visibility NoVisualChange
checkpoint no_visual_change
quit
